  "contract": [
    "Mask bytes other than exactly1 copy raw sample bits, including0xff. A marked positive or negative sample clears its complete sign run by backward/forward scans with live reads. Marked zeros and NaNs leave output unchanged; destination memory is not globally initialized. Preserve writes that may change subsequent samples or mask bytes.",
    "Comparison is native VCMPE.F32 against zero: unordered raises IOC for all NaNs and sets unordered NZCV; FZ denormals raise IDC and compare as signed zero without rewriting input memory. Ordinary integer C plus FPSCR intrinsics preserve the status/branch behavior without inline assembly.",
    "Scale/copy writes factor1 before dispatch. Mode1 then writes factor1.5 and multiplies sequential samples by the native125-value periodic window; other modes call actual C memmove, preserving overlaps. The60-byte scale entry and26-byte shared tail have one C provider.",
    "All500 coefficient bytes are explicit non-executable data in the C object. The observed spectral caller uses125 samples. Ghidra only defines an undefined4 at the table address; no broader array layout or modes beyond the observed contract are inferred. No writable owner is added."
  ],
